From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] i18n: honor DESTDIR in custom install copies

Meson runs custom install scripts with DESTDIR set to the packaging root.
The paths computed here are absolute installation paths, so prefix both the
generated catalog source and each bundled plugin destination with DESTDIR.
Without this, RPM builds look for the catalog below the build host's /usr and
attempt to install plugin translations outside the buildroot.

Upstream replaced this loop after v3.0.1 with an installer based on
MESON_INSTALL_DESTDIR_PREFIX (commit f38a155f9168a29460380642b4f1cbcc81a5186b).
This minimal equivalent preserves the stable release's generated catalogs and
plugin layout.
---
 po/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/po/meson.build b/po/meson.build
index be35560..0baa37a 100644
--- a/po/meson.build
+++ b/po/meson.build
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ foreach language_tag : resynthesizer_i18n_languages
     # cp does not have option to create destination dirs, so create directory first.
     meson.add_install_script(
       'sh', '-c',
-      'mkdir -p "@0@" && cp -f "@1@" "@2@"'.format(dest_dir, source_file, dest_file ))
+      'mkdir -p "$DESTDIR@0@" && cp -f "$DESTDIR@1@" "$DESTDIR@2@"'.format(dest_dir, source_file, dest_file ))
 
   endforeach
 endforeach
